lines+=sect(10,'Robustness findings','Repetition is concentrated in upper-tier grammars: technology versus rate effects, budget financing recognition, and simple subtraction of projected debt ratios. These are chiefly classified F because strong Hard coverage already exists. Targeted inverse, conditional and reconciliation tasks replace selected repeated forms. The near-duplicate Medium/Hard pair 43318/43317 is separated by retaining the Medium direction question and giving Hard a quantity-identification requirement. Some direct upper items and simple distractors remain; a mature-bank audit does not justify rewriting every usable variant.')
lines+=sect(11,'Calibration findings','No systemic C gap was found. The 58 canonical Hard records already include multi-transaction classification, component arithmetic, planned-market disequilibrium, graph causation, fiscal chains and denominator comparisons. **52 retain their question content**; six receive corrections or a more substantive application. Elite/Legendary revisions account for 23 of the 30 content changes. No difficulty metadata or pool tier changed.')
lines+=sect(12,'Numerical and integration findings','Twenty-two revised numerical records were independently recomputed from final staged stems with rational arithmetic. Graph interpolation uses coordinates transcribed from the inspected images, not old answers. The verifier covers all revised numerical items, including changes limited to assumptions. Every selected record has four distinct normalized options and exactly one matching answer hash; revised alternatives were also reviewed for economic uniqueness.','Representative results: 43205 has realized saving/investment of 220 and unplanned inventory investment of −30; 43070 reconciles a 180 deficit, 230 net issuance, 3,830 ending debt and 50 cash growth; 43098 gives textbook public saving of 60 versus a full-budget deficit of 10 under the explicitly stated interest convention; 43145 gives 32 interest outlays and a 12 increase in the deficit. Full final inputs, derivations and keyed alternatives are in `numerical-validation.json`.')
lines+=sect(13,'Graph-use findings','Meaningful graph use was already present; no E coverage gap was found. All **8 registered image files** were visually inspected. All **60 graph-linked records** remain linked; **59** remain Trial-by-Graph eligible (15 Easy, 19 Medium, 16 Hard, 5 Elite, 4 Legendary). Eligibility flags were not changed to improve audit counts.','The revised graph problems distinguish the full horizontal curve shift from the smaller equilibrium-quantity response, infer an undrawn demand curve, and reconstruct fiscal/private-saving offsets. Every graph byte and registered path remains unchanged. The generated-game browser check renders all 60 images, opens every enlargement and verifies description delivery. Eight contracts have corrected or expanded visual evidence. No new graphs were needed.')
lines+=sect(14,'Upper-tier synthesis findings','Selective Elite/Legendary improvements require inventory reconciliation, reverse demand reconstruction, fixed-rate versus realized saving decomposition, debt issuance versus principal rollover and cash balances, budget versus GDP classification, refinancing exposure, and denominator thresholds. These tasks use introductory selected models without importing corporate valuation or monetary stabilization.','Not every retained upper record now exceeds ordinary exam demand: 43120 and 43166 remain direct measure-comparison/checklist items; 43285 remains a compact simultaneous-shift application. These are residual calibration limitations disclosed rather than hidden through retagging or wholesale replacement.')
lines+=sect(15,'Strong existing Hard questions retained','Examples below retain stems, options, feedback and answer keys. Graph examples may receive accessibility-only changes. The complete 52-ID retained-content list is in `retained-hard.json`.')
