lines+=sect(17,'Economic and numerical defects corrected','43205 no longer describes S=I as merely an equilibrium relationship; 43231 explicitly separates always-valid realized accounting, including inventories, from planned imbalances. 43203 and 43210 now distinguish changes in schedules at a given rate from final realized saving, avoiding a false fixed-quantity inference in simultaneous-shift scenarios.','43098 defines gross taxes, transfers, purchases and interest before comparing public saving with the full budget. 43134 states the borrowing-finance assumption before connecting a deficit to the debt stock. The graph reconstructions give an explicit currency scale when dollar magnitudes matter and derive shift sizes from the actual straight lines. 43162 removes an unstable dataset “last updated” claim while retaining its dated-stock interpretation. No reversed graph key or image-byte defect was found in this pool.','The February 2026 CBO figures remain explicitly historical projections: revenues/outlays of 5.6/7.4 trillion, a separately rounded 1.9 trillion deficit, debt ratios of 101/120 percent, and rising interest outlays. The report itself warns that rounded components may not sum to totals; retained rounded-value questions are not erroneous for that reason. New ratio exercises use displayed values and label their conditional calculations. [CBO February 2026 baseline](https://www.cbo.gov/publication/62105).','Debt measures and dated stock observations retain their distinct Treasury meanings. No live debt amount was substituted into the bank. Treasury’s official reporting pages distinguish debt held by the public, intragovernmental holdings and debt-limit measures, and provide dated debt history. [Treasury debt reporting](https://www.treasurydirect.gov/government/public-debt-reports/debt-position-and-activity-report/), [Treasury debt history](https://www.treasurydirect.gov/mobile/).')
lines+=sect(18,'Accessibility and paths','All eight shared contracts now describe axes, the actual printed curve labels, straight-line coordinates, marked intersections and applicable guides/grid. Only LOANABLE-01 visibly prints saving/investment parentheticals; other contracts use their actual S/D labels. LOANABLE-06 no longer names the crowding-out conclusion. LOANABLE-08 no longer performs the quantity-change subtraction. Evidence permits reconstruction without supplying the assessed economic inference.','All 60 inline graph contracts are synchronized: seven coincide with content changes and 53 are accessibility-only. There are **zero path fixes, zero path-only records and zero new or altered image files**. The initial intersection evidence on LOANABLE-01 was accurate and was retained with additional line coordinates needed for the revised calculations. Detailed metadata was not shortened merely because of length.')
lines+=sect(19,'Final-exam calibration','The supplied ECO 2251 Final Exam was used only for cognitive/style calibration. Its bytes match the previously inspected exam. Q23 supports ordinary causal reasoning from a fiscal change through financing conditions to private investment at Hard. Q30 supplies only the boundary reminder that investment responds to rates; its AD-AS/stabilization chain was not imported.','The exam does not define selected objectives or supply templates. New records use independent budget constraints, inventory accounting, actual existing library graphs and reverse ratio tests. No exam question, answer pattern or image was copied, renamed or revalued. A 12-word screening comparison of revised stems, options and feedback finds no new overlap; this supplements human task comparison and is not treated as proof of originality. See `originality-validation.json`.')
