lines+=sect(22,'Remaining warnings and review flags',f"Existing auditor: before **{before['counts']['errors']} errors / {before['counts']['warnings']} warnings / {before['counts']['reviews']} reviews**; after **{after['counts']['errors']} errors / {after['counts']['warnings']} warnings / {after['counts']['reviews']} reviews**. The final 25 reviews comprise 23 absolute-distractor flags and two difficulty-overstatement flags. Every before/final record-rule pair has an individual disposition in `quality-dispositions.json`; no rules were disabled or edited.",'43219 is a regex false positive: the task requires inverse line reconstruction, despite the checker not recognizing “inferred” as its “infer” cue. 43249 is a modest inverse graph application at the easier edge of Hard and remains flagged. Some absolute alternatives meaningfully express misconceptions; others remain weak elimination cues. The report does not equate zero errors with perfect distractors or uniformly deep upper tiers.')
