lines+=sect(23,'Remaining limitations','This is a content and delivery audit, not an empirical item-discrimination or student-performance study. Some retained direct upper-tier questions, similar introductory grammars and easy-to-eliminate alternatives remain. Adequate Hard applications were preserved rather than rewritten for stylistic uniformity.','The existing linear loanable-funds and simplified fiscal accounting models are instructional assumptions. Other valid textbook conventions were not imposed. Detailed graph evidence can legitimately make basic coordinate questions easy for any learner; accessibility was not weakened to make them harder. Direct Fiscal Data pages returned access errors during this session, so official Treasury reporting/history pages supplied the accessible cross-check; no current daily amount is claimed.','Validation is local: all-mode composition readiness, unchanged routing, independent revised arithmetic, complete graph rendering/enlargement and generated payload checks. No claim is made about untested full gameplay branches or remote CDN state. Production changes remain local and require no deployment, commit, merge or push in this task.')
lines+=sect(24,'Final semantic library hash',f"**`{semantic}`**",f"BEFORE: `{old['librarySha256']}`. The semantic SHA-256 was independently recomputed using sorted canonical JSON with the two self-referential hash fields excluded. Library, registry and manifest agree. Only `build/faculty-build-composer/data/composer_library.js`, `composer_registry.json` and `composer_library_manifest.json` are changed for this audit; the sidecars synchronize required hashes and existing asset-accessibility metadata.")
(W/'FINAL_REPORT.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n','utf8')
